cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "rldoctor: diagnostics for GRPO/RLVR training runs"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: junglezke
repository-code: "https://github.com/junglezke/rldoctor"
abstract: >-
  rldoctor reads the metric log of a reinforcement-learning post-training run and
  reports which documented failure mode it is exhibiting, what that failure has cost
  in GPU-hours, and what configuration change addresses it. It covers zero-variance
  GRPO groups, entropy collapse, reward/eval divergence, length hacking, truncation,
  clip saturation, KL drift, gradient pathologies, reward-component imbalance and
  learning plateaus, working from logs produced by verl, TRL, or any training loop,
  with no instrumentation required.
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - RLHF
  - RLVR
  - GRPO
  - large language models
  - training diagnostics
  - reward hacking
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
